<title>SWEDEN: TABLE-INCENTIVE H1 PROFIT 11.74 BLN SKR.</title>
<headline>TABLE-INCENTIVE H1 PROFIT 11.74 BLN SKR.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish medial technology and investment group Incentive AB on Monday posted these earnings for the first six months of the year, ending on June 30.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit after fin items		 11,735 vs  1,989</p>
<p> Sales					10,309 vs 10,639</p>
<p> One-off items			    11,101 vs    670</p>
<p> EPS (Skr)				  143.49 vs  14.86</p>
<p>Operating costs, including</p>
<p> one-off items		   CREDIT  1,441 vs  9,034 CHARGE</p>
<p> Goodwill depreciation		     405 vs    280</p>
<p> Other depreciation			  438 vs    389</p>
<p> Operating profit			 11,750 vs  1,605</p>
<p> Net financial items	    CHARGE    15 vs    384 CREDIT</p>
<p> Minorities				     12 vs    106</p>
<p> Tax					   1,912 vs    867</p>
<p> Net profit				  9,811 vs  1,016</p>
<p>NOTE -- Market expectations were for a profit after financial items of 11.70 billion crowns, including a capital gain of 11.20 billion crowns, a Reuters poll of nine analysts found.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
